==English==

===Alternative forms===
* {{l|en|Mogor}} {{defdate|16th-17th}}
* {{l|en|Mogul}}
* {{l|en|Mughal}}

===Etymology===
Ultimately from {{etyl|ur|en}} {{m|ur|مغل|tr=muġal}}, variant of {{m|ur|مغل|tr=muġul}}, from {{etyl|fa|en}} {{m|fa|مغول|tr=muġul}}, from {{etyl|mn|en}} {{m|mn|ᠮᠣᠩᠭᠣᠯ|tr=mongɣol}}. In early use via various European languages.{{attention|ur}} {{attention|mn}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# A head of the Mongolian [[dynasty]] founded by Zahīr-ud-Dīn Muhammed Bābur (1483-1530) which controlled large parts of southern Asia from the 16th to the 19th centuries.
# {{lb|en|now|_|historical}} A [[Mongol]] or [[Mongolian]], especially a member or follower of the Moghul dynasty.
# An [[important]] or [[successful]] person; a [[magnate]]. (Now usually as {{term|mogul}})

